The legal text is from the statutes published by the Office of the Legislative Counsel, Nova Scotia House of Assembly
(https://nslegislature.ca): the Interpretation Act, the Human Rights Act and the Limitation of Actions Act, read from
Internet Archive captures of 18 April 2026 and retrieved 29 October 2026. Each statute page says it is provided "for
your convenience and personal use only", may not be copied for resale, and that official sources should be consulted
where accuracy is critical. Lexifina's copy is free to read and is not sold.

Changes made by Lexifina: the HTML was converted to one Markdown file per section; the amendment citations after each
section, capital-letter part headings and layout were removed. The wording of the law was not changed. The Province of
Nova Scotia does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages and the tools) are dedicated to the
public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
